---
alwaysApply: true
---
description: Rules to optimize performance of React and TypeScript components.
globs: **/*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx}
---
- Optimize React component rendering using memoization techniques (e.g., React.memo).
- Avoid unnecessary re-renders.
- Lazy load components and images when possible.
- Heavy editors (e.g. TipTap / rich markdown) should load via `React.lazy` + `Suspense` so initial routes stay small.
- Use efficient data structures and algorithms.
- Zustand selectors must return stable references when store data is unchanged (avoid `Object.values`/new arrays in the selector body); see `dom-state-shadcn-pitfalls.mdc`.